  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": 13775,
      "content": "On Thursday, October 1 at 11:54 p.m. ET Falcon Heavy launched the <a href=\"https://sxcontent9668.azureedge.us/cms-assets/assets/NROL_97_141eb4af0c.png\" target=\"_\">NROL-97</a> mission from Launch Complex 39A (LC-39A) at NASA\u2019s Kennedy Space Center in Florida."
    },
    {
      "id": 13776,
      "content": "This was the second and fourth flight for the two first stage side boosters supporting this mission, which previously launched the <a href=\"https://www.spacex.com/launches/goes-u\" target=\"_\">GOES-U</a>, <a href=\"https://www.spacex.com/launches/viasat3f3\" target=\"_\">Viasat-3 F3</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.spacex.com/launches/roman\" target=\"_\">Roman Space Telescope</a> missions. Following stage separation, Falcon Heavy\u2019s two side boosters landed on SpaceX\u2019s Landing Zones 1 and 2 (LZ-1 and LZ-2) at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida."
    }
  ]
